+## Domain reputation policy and settings
+
+Every distinct domain in a message is looked up with
+`GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/{domain}` (key in the `x-apikey`
+header; existing reports only, nothing is submitted for scanning, and the
+user-supplied URL is never fetched). Defaults are conservative and configurable
+through environment variables read at server startup:
+
+| Variable | Default | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `VIRUSTOTAL_API_KEY` | unset | Required for lookups. Never logged or returned to clients. |
+| `REPUTATION_MALICIOUS_THRESHOLD` | `1` | Malicious detections at or above this block with `malicious_domain`. |
+| `REPUTATION_SUSPICIOUS_THRESHOLD` | `1` | Suspicious detections at or above this block with `suspicious_domain`. |
+| `REPUTATION_MAX_REPORT_AGE_SECONDS` | `604800` (7 days) | Reports older than this are stale → `reputation_unknown`. |
+| `REPUTATION_MAX_DOMAINS_PER_MESSAGE` | `5` | Extra domains beyond this are dropped, not checked. |
+| `REPUTATION_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS` | `900` | How long a verdict is reused before re-querying. |
+| `REPUTATION_CACHE_MAX_SIZE` | `512` | Bounded LRU cache of domain verdicts. |
+| `REPUTATION_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` | `10` | Per-lookup timeout; there are no retries. |
+| `REPUTATION_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE` | `4` | Local budget matching VirusTotal's free public API. |
+| `REPUTATION_COOLDOWN_SECONDS` | `60` | Pause after an HTTP 429 before trying again. |
+| `VIRUSTOTAL_API_BASE_URL` | official endpoint | Only for tests pointing at a mock server. |
+
+Decision order per domain: malicious → `malicious_domain`; suspicious →
+`suspicious_domain`; then a report must be recent **and** contain at least one
+harmless verdict to be allowed; anything else (no timestamp, stale, undetected-only,
+404, missing key, timeout, HTTP/auth error, 429, malformed JSON) is
+`reputation_unknown` and rejected. Missing verification is never treated as safety.
+Simultaneous lookups for the same domain share one HTTP request.
+
+Reputation limitations: bare mentions without `http(s)://` or `www.` are only
+recognized for a curated list of common TLDs (see `reputation.py`) to avoid treating
+`config.yml` or `node.js` as domains, so obscure-TLD bare mentions are missed while
+prefixed links are always checked. IP-address links and internal hostnames
+(`localhost`, `*.local`, `*.internal`, `*.lan`, `*.home`, `*.corp`, `*.test`,
+`*.invalid`, `*.example`, `*.localdomain`) are skipped, not looked up. The exact
+parsed hostname is checked (`paypal.com.evil.tld` is never trusted because it
+contains `paypal.com`), but a subdomain may have no report of its own and will then
+be rejected as unknown. IDNA uses Python's built-in codec, not full IDNA2008/UTS-46.
+The local rate counter only sees this process; other applications sharing the same
+key can still trigger VirusTotal throttling, which is handled by the 429 cooldown.
+Domains beyond the per-message limit are silently unchecked. Verdicts are cached
+in memory only and reset on restart.
+
